      "message": "By the way I encourage you to take a look to the diff between this patchset (or patchset 25) and patchset 26.\n\nIt turns out that ps24 and 25 are mightily flaky :\n```\n[1/3] com.android.server.connectivity.MultinetworkPolicyTrackerTest#testUpdateAvoidBadWifi: FAILED (361ms)\n\nSTACKTRACE:\norg.mockito.exceptions.misusing.UnfinishedStubbingException: \nUnfinished stubbing detected here:\n-\u003e at \ncom.android.server.connectivity.MultinetworkPolicyTrackerTest.testUpdateAvoidBadWifi(MultinetworkPolicyTrackerTest.kt:128)\n\nE.g. thenReturn() may be missing.\nExamples of correct stubbing:\n    when(mock.isOk()).thenReturn(true);\n    when(mock.isOk()).thenThrow(exception);\n    doThrow(exception).when(mock).someVoidMethod();\nHints:\n 1. missing thenReturn()\n 2. you are trying to stub a final method, which is not supported\n 3: you are stubbing the behaviour of another mock inside before \u0027thenReturn\u0027 instruction if completed\n\n            at \ncom.android.server.connectivity.MultinetworkPolicyTrackerTest.testUpdateAvoidBadWifi(MultinetworkPolicyTrackerTest.kt:128)\n```\n\nWhere l.128 is :\n\n    doReturn(0).`when`(resources).getInteger(R.integer.config_activelyPreferBadWifi)\n\nThis is happening because in another thread we have calls to getInteger on the mock ...and evidently mockito\u0027s mocks are just not thread-safe, even if you don\u0027t call when().thenReturn, of which there are none in this test.",
